SUMMARY: I Love From Memory\, a solo show by Nate Orton
DESCRIPTION:#art-opening #gallery #artistreception #paintings #collectors
 \n\nIn I love from memory\, Nate Orton presents a new body of paintings\,
  woodburns\, and books rooted in close observation and the quiet persiste
 nce of memory. Working from a pocket sketchbook\, Orton captures fleeting
  scenes from daily life… a cloud over a parking lot\, light across a stan
 d of trees\, moments that might otherwise go unnoticed but continue to li
 nger long after they pass.\n\nHe returns to these scenes repeatedly\, bot
 h in person and in memory\, redrawing and refining them over time. Throug
 h this process\, compositions shift and simplify\, distilling each image 
 to its most essential forms\, colors\, and symbols. What begins as observ
 ation gradually becomes something more reflective and interior.\n\nIn the
  studio\, these drawings evolve into casein tempera paintings\, built thr
 ough layered applications of a fast-drying\, traditional medium. The resu
 lting works move beyond documentation\, becoming meditations on memory\, 
 time\, and place.\n\nOrton’s practice began in North Central Idaho\, wher
 e he made work along creeks\, rivers\, and canyons. Now based in Milwauki
 e\, Oregon\, he continues to walk and draw regularly\, finding a quiet ki
 nd of strangeness and beauty in the suburban landscape around him.
CATEGORIES:art,gallery-opening
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62191926b9407b
 526addc41f/69c7022d701bd67bec4efdc4/scaled_640.jpg
