SUMMARY: Celebrate National Train Day at the Oregon Rail Heritage Center
DESCRIPTION:National Train Day: May 9 & 10\, 10:00am-6:00pm\n\nGet ready 
 for two full days of steam\, history\, and railroad excitement at the Ore
 gon Rail Heritage Center’s annual National Train Day Celebration! This ye
 ar\, we’re going bigger—with two action-packed days of family fun\, histo
 ric locomotives\, and unforgettable railroading experiences\, on Saturday
 \, May 9 and Sunday\, May 10.\n\nThere will be something for everyone to 
 enjoy\, including:\n\n  * SP 4449 and SP&S 700 under steam\n  * Cab tours
  of these legendary locomotives\n  * Turntable demonstrations\n  * Model 
 railroad displays from local clubs and enthusiasts\n  * Food trucks and r
 efreshments\n  * Family-friendly activities\n  * Opportunities to explore
  the museum and rail yard\n  * And plenty of railroading excitement all w
 eekend long!\n\nWant to make your Train Day visit even more memorable? Ho
 p aboard for a steam-powered excursion behind the historic Polson #2 loco
 motive and enjoy a ride you won’t soon forget.\n\nGeneral admission for T
 rain Day festivities is $5 per person and free for infants under 3 and OR
 HC members. Train rides start at $25 for adults and $15 for children and 
 include event admission.\n\nFor more information and to purchase tickets\
 , visit https://orhf.org/blog/national-train-day-returns-may-9-10-2026/ h
 ttps://orhf.org/blog/national-train-day-returns-may-9-10-2026/ .\n\nDon’t
  miss one of Portland’s most exciting and historic events of the year—com
 e see\, hear\, and ride living railroad history!
CATEGORIES:Train-Day,Trains,Train-Ride,Kid-Friendly
