SUMMARY: 2026 Northwest Horn Society Symposium
DESCRIPTION:The School of Music & Theater at Portland State University is
  pleased to host the 2026 Northwest Horn Symposium on April 10–12\, 2026.
  With generous additional support from the Northwest Horn Society\, the e
 vent will feature concerts\, masterclasses\, lectures\, competitions and 
 playing opportunities for hornists of all ages and experiences.\n\nDavid 
 Byrd-Marrow (Oberlin College) will be the guest artist for the event. His
  interactive recital will engage with the theme of this year’s symposium\
 , “Esprit de Cors\,” a general theme to help unify talks\, performances a
 nd presentations.\n\nThe event will also feature the Oregon Symphony’s Su
 nday matinee of Ravel’s Daphnis et Chloé. Also on the program are Saint-S
 aëns’s Le Rouet d’Omphale and Ravel’s Piano Concerto\, featuring Ingrid F
 liter. Special student and adult registrant pricing will be available.\n\
 nThe event will also feature regional horn artists as performers and pres
 enters\, and provide a wide range of activities for all hornists\, from b
 eginners to professionals.\n\nGraphic by Li Kuang.
CATEGORIES:music,workshops,masterclasses,horn
