SUMMARY: 56th Cowlitz Coin Club Coin Show
DESCRIPTION:The Cowlitz Coin Club of Longview-Kelso is celebrating its 56
 th coin show on April 26 at the AWPPW Hall\, located at 724 15th Avenue i
 n Longview.\n\nShow hours are 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, and admission\, parking
  and dealer appraisals are all free.\n\nAt the show\, the public can buy\
 , sell and trade coins\, currency\, tokens and medals from numerous Pacif
 ic Northwest dealers.\n\nThere will be drawings\, along with a raffle for
  a half-ounce American Gold Eagle coin and five one-ounce American Silver
  Eagle coins. You do not need to be present to win the raffle coins.\n\nT
 he Cowlitz Coin Club\, a member of the American Numismatic Association\, 
 is a non-profit educational organization dedicated to promoting\, extendi
 ng and protecting the interests of numismatics and its activities through
 out the Pacific Northwest. Its goal is to foster and encourage the study 
 of numismatics in all its forms and branches.\n\nThe Cowlitz Coin Club me
 ets at 7 p.m. on the third Saturday of each month at the Catlin Center\, 
 located at 106 NW 8th Ave. in Kelso\, Wash. (adjacent to the Kelso Spray 
 Park).\n\nFor additional information about club meetings\, email cowlitzc
 oinclublongview@gmail.com mailto:cowlitzcoinclublongview@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:
