SUMMARY: Well of Hope concert to benefit Hopewell House
DESCRIPTION:On Sunday\, May 3\, 2026\, at 4:00 p.m.\, the acclaimed Marsh
 -Titterington Piano Duo will present a special benefit concert for Hopewe
 ll House at Lincoln Hall 75.\n\nThis inspiring afternoon of music will fe
 ature dynamic and expressive works by Piazzolla\, Copland\, Marsh\, and G
 ershwin\, offering an energizing and memorable experience for all who att
 end.\n\nThe concert supports Hopewell House\, Portland’s only residential
  care home solely dedicated to compassionate end-of-life care for all. Pr
 oceeds from the event will help sustain the organization’s mission of pro
 viding dignity\, comfort\, and support to individuals and families during
  one of life’s most important transitions.\n\nPianists Lisa Marsh and Con
 nie Titterington\, professors at Portland State University\, have perform
 ed together for more than 20 years and are celebrated for their artistry\
 , connection\, and vibrant performances.\n\nGeneral admission tickets are
  $25.\nSponsor levels with reserved seating are also available.\n\nTicket
 s may be purchased in advance at: https://hopewellhousepdx.org https://ho
 pewellhousepdx.org
CATEGORIES:Piano,concert,Hopewell-House
